-- ============================================================
-- Migration 141: what other sites name in London (first city).
-- (Applied automatically by the build; nothing to paste.)
--
-- Jonathan, 5 Oct 2026: review competitor websites and leading blogs
-- that mention cafes and coworking spaces, then screen them to make
-- sure they are still open. He chose London first, and laptop-cafe
-- directories, coworking directories and city blogs and magazines.
--
-- Read on 5 Oct 2026 by a session: 38 sites, 1096 mentions of 845
-- places (names, the neighbourhood or address a site gives, and where
-- it was read; no text of theirs). Loaded with the functions of
-- migration 140. From tonight the nightly job matches each name to a
-- place and checks it is still open, the most named first, within the
-- plan of migration 140 (to start: 40 lookups a day, and only names
-- that two sites or one trusted list give, 257 of the 845).
--
-- Weight 2 is a hand-picked list from a known publisher; weight 1 an
-- ordinary list or directory. Two sites that were read are left out
-- as too loose to count (Cafe Nomad and Downunder Cafe: unfiltered
-- lists with airport outlets and a Hard Rock Cafe), and so is
-- Workfrom (nothing newer than 2017). Coworker.com could not be read.
--
-- To strike a site later: update public.mention_sources set weight =
-- 0 where source = '...'; its mentions then count for nothing.
--
-- Nothing here writes to a space or the website.
-- ============================================================

